        ":activity/steps": [
          {
            ":db/id": 17592186101854,
            ":step/content": {
              ":db/id": 17592186101952,
              ":tutorial/content": "Suppose we are given the following matrix:\n\n<div class=\"matrix-operands matrix-operands-stacked\">\n<div>$A =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}$</div>\n</div>\n\nWe denote the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}3$rd row and $\\color{red}2$nd column using the notation $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}.$\n\nThe first subscript represents the row and the second subscript represents the column. So $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}=8,$ as shown below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & \\boxed{8} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can denote every entry of a matrix in this way.\nFor instance, $a_{{\\color{blue}4}\\color{red}1}$ denotes the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}4$th row and $\\color{red}1$st column.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33} \\\\ {a}_{41} & {a}_{42} & {a}_{43}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
              ":tutorial/id": "34f3a63d-a273-50fb-b26a-ae172c7e93e9",
              ":tutorial/math-academy-id": 2969,
              ":tutorial/title": "Introduction"
            },
            ":step/id": "71c4da2c-9ba7-5b55-a1fc-62db722468f0",
            ":step/math-academy-id": 462030,
            ":step/next": {
